request.toUri()` (now carrying both `ui_locales` and `hl`).\n\n**Explicitly out of scope:**\n- Upstream `OAuthGoogle.kt` / `OAuthFastmail.kt` — not used on the device (Custom Tabs path); left untouched per the Kompakt no-upstream-edits convention.\n- `KompaktOAuthWebViewActivity` — no WebView/`Accept-Language` changes. If on-device testing shows Google *still* forces English despite `hl`, the documented fallback is to also set the WebView `Accept-Language` (the original Approach 3), added then — not pre-emptively (YAGNI).\n\n**Success criteria:**\n1. `./gradlew :core:compileDebugKotlin` passes.\n2. On device with phone language = Polish (or another shipped, Google-supported language): *Link account* → the Google login WebView renders in that language. Same when re-authorizing an existing account.\n3. The built auth URL contains `hl=<tag>` (inspectable via a one-off log if needed).\n\nDoes this design look right? If so, I'll write it up as a spec doc under `docs/superpowers/specs/` and commit it for your review before we move to a plan.",
