            "content": "# Localize Google OAuth login WebView (hl parameter) — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make the embedded Google sign-in WebView render in the phone's language by adding Google's `hl` URL parameter to the OAuth authorization request.\n\n**Architecture:** `KompaktGoogleLoginViewModel.signIn()` already passes the device locale tag into `KompaktOAuthGoogle.signIn()`, which builds an AppAuth `AuthorizationRequest` and sets the OIDC `ui_locales` hint. We add Google's own `hl` parameter (which Google honors across its whole multi-page flow) as a custom AppAuth additional parameter, reusing the same locale tag. The WebView (`KompaktOAuthWebViewActivity`) loads `request.toUri()`, so the new parameter rides along with no WebView changes. The same `signIn()` serves both the initial-link and re-auth flows.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Kotlin, AppAuth (`net.openid:appauth` 0.11.1), JUnit4 + Robolectric 4.16.1 for the unit test.\n\n## Global Constraints\n\n- Kotlin only — no new Java files.\n- Kompakt fork convention: modify **only** Kompakt-prefixed files. Touch `KompaktOAuthGoogle.kt` only; leave upstream `OAuthGoogle.kt` / `OAuthFastmail.kt` untouched.\n- Keep the existing `.setUiLocales(locale)` call — remove no behavior.\n- `hl` value is the **full BCP-47 tag** already passed in (e.g. `pl-PL`, `pt-BR`) — the same `locale` string, not a truncated language subtag.\n- Only attach `hl` when `locale != null`.\n- Branch: `task/SHP-570` (from `kompakt`). Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-29-google-oauth-webview-locale-design.md`.\n- Core unit tests that touch `android.net.Uri` must run under Robolectric with `@ConscryptMode(ConscryptMode.Mode.OFF)` (the app uses Conscrypt; unit tests do not).\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Add `hl` to the Google authorization request\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `core/src/main/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogle.kt` (the `signIn` function, currently lines 32–44)\n- Test: `core/src/test/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogleTest.kt` (create)\n\n**Interfaces:**\n- Consumes: `KompaktOAuthGoogle(oAuthIntegration: OAuthIntegration)`; `OAuthIntegration(context: Context)`; `KompaktOAuthGoogle.signIn(email: String?, customClientId: String?, locale: String?): net.openid.appauth.AuthorizationRequest`.\n- Produces: an `AuthorizationRequest` whose public `additionalParameters: Map<String, String>` contains `\"hl\" -> locale` when `locale != null`, and no `\"hl\"` key when `locale == null`. `ui_locales` continues to be set via the existing `setUiLocales`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nCreate `core/src/test/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogleTest.kt`:\n\n```kotlin\n/*\n * Copyright © All Contributors. See LICENSE and AUTHORS in the root directory for details.\n */\n\npackage at.bitfire.davdroid.network\n\nimport org.junit.Assert.assertEquals\nimport org.junit.Assert.assertFalse\nimport org.junit.Test\nimport org.junit.runner.RunWith\nimport org.robolectric.RobolectricTestRunner\nimport org.robolectric.RuntimeEnvironment\nimport org.robolectric.annotation.ConscryptMode\n\n@RunWith(RobolectricTestRunner::class)\n@ConscryptMode(ConscryptMode.Mode.OFF)      // app uses Conscrypt; unit tests do not\nclass KompaktOAuthGoogleTest {\n\n    private val oAuthGoogle = KompaktOAuthGoogle(\n        OAuthIntegration(RuntimeEnvironment.getApplication())\n    )\n\n    @Test\n    fun `signIn adds hl parameter from locale`() {\n        val request = oAuthGoogle.signIn(email = \"user@gmail.com\", customClientId = null, locale = \"pl-PL\")\n        assertEquals(\"pl-PL\", request.additionalParameters[\"hl\"])\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `signIn keeps ui_locales hint`() {\n        val request = oAuthGoogle.signIn(email = \"user@gmail.com\", customClientId = null, locale = \"pl-PL\")\n        assertEquals(\"pl-PL\", request.uiLocales)\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `signIn without locale omits hl parameter`() {\n        val request = oAuthGoogle.signIn(email = \"user@gmail.com\", customClientId = null, locale = null)\n        assertFalse(request.additionalParameters.containsKey(\"hl\"))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run the test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `./gradlew :core:testDebugUnitTest --tests \"at.bitfire.davdroid.network.KompaktOAuthGoogleTest\"`\nExpected: FAIL on `signIn adds hl parameter from locale` — `expected:<pl-PL> but was:<null>` (the request has no `hl` yet). The other two tests pass already (they assert existing/absent behavior).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the `hl` parameter in `signIn`**\n\nIn `core/src/main/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogle.kt`, replace the body of `signIn` (currently):\n\n```kotlin\n    fun signIn(email: String?, customClientId: String?, locale: String?): AuthorizationRequest {\n        val builder = AuthorizationRequest.Builder(\n            serviceConfig,\n            customClientId ?: CLIENT_ID,\n            ResponseTypeValues.CODE,\n            oAuthIntegration.redirectUri\n        )\n        return builder\n            .setScopes(*SCOPES)\n            .setLoginHint(email)\n            .setUiLocales(locale)\n            .build()\n    }\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```kotlin\n    fun signIn(email: String?, customClientId: String?, locale: String?): AuthorizationRequest {\n        val builder = AuthorizationRequest.Builder(\n            serviceConfig,\n            customClientId ?: CLIENT_ID,\n            ResponseTypeValues.CODE,\n            oAuthIntegration.redirectUri\n        )\n            .setScopes(*SCOPES)\n            .setLoginHint(email)\n            .setUiLocales(locale)\n        if (locale != null)\n            // Google's own UI-language switch; honored across the whole multi-page sign-in,\n            // unlike the ui_locales hint above. \"hl\" is a custom (non-OIDC) param, so AppAuth\n            // accepts it via setAdditionalParameters.\n            builder.setAdditionalParameters(mapOf(\"hl\" to locale))\n        return builder.build()\n    }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run the test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `./gradlew :core:testDebugUnitTest --tests \"at.bitfire.davdroid.network.KompaktOAuthGoogleTest\"`\nExpected: PASS (all three tests).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Compile-check the module**\n\nRun: `./gradlew :core:compileDebugKotlin`\nExpected: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add core/src/main/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogle.kt \\\n        core/src/test/kotlin/at/bitfire/davdroid/network/KompaktOAuthGoogleTest.kt\ngit commit -m \"[SHP-570] Localize Google OAuth WebView via hl parameter\n\nAdd Google's hl URL parameter to the OAuth authorization request,\nalongside the existing ui_locales hint, so the embedded sign-in WebView\nrenders in the phone language. Covers both initial link and re-auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Manual on-device verification (not automatable)\n\nAfter Task 1, verify the real behavior the bug is about (spec success criterion 2):\n\n1. Set the device language to a shipped, Google-supported language (e.g. Polish).\n2. In DAVx⁵: *Link account* → choose Google → the embedded Google sign-in WebView should render in that language.\n3. Trigger a re-authorization of an existing Google account (`KompaktReauthScreen`) → the WebView should also render in that language.\n\nIf Google **still** forces English despite `hl`, escalate per the spec's fallback: also set the WebView's `Accept-Language` on the initial load in `KompaktOAuthWebViewActivity`. Do not implement that pre-emptively.\n\n## Self-Review\n\n- **Spec coverage:** The spec's single change (add `hl` in `KompaktOAuthGoogle.signIn`, keep `ui_locales`, guard on `locale != null`, full BCP-47 tag) is implemented in Task 1, Step 